T*
(### `optimize\(...\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(This is the main orchestration method. It:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Loads the current holdings.) Tj
T*
(2. Validates that holdings exist.) Tj
T*
(3. Reads user preferences from the request.) Tj
T*
(4. Calculates current portfolio value.) Tj
T*
(5. Adds available cash to determine investable value.) Tj
T*
(6. Builds asset-level metrics.) Tj
T*
(7. Selects the best assets based on score.) Tj
T*
(8. Computes target allocation weights.) Tj
T*
(9. Builds:) Tj
T*
(   - current allocations) Tj
T*
(   - optimized allocations) Tj
T*
(   - buy/sell/hold recommendations) Tj
T*
(10. Calculates:) Tj
T*
(   - expected return) Tj
T*
(   - expected risk) Tj
T*
(   - Sharpe ratio) Tj
T*
(11. Returns the final response DTO.) Tj
T*
T*
(### `buildAssetMetrics\(...\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(This method creates a scoreable record for each holding. For each asset it calculates:) Tj
T*
T*
(- current value) Tj
T*
(- current portfolio weight) Tj
T*
(- expected return) Tj
T*
(- risk score) Tj
T*
(- final optimization score) Tj
T*
T*
(The core scoring idea is:) Tj
T*
T*
(`score = adjusted return - \(lambda x adjusted risk\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(So:) Tj
T*
T*
(- higher return improves the score) Tj
T*
(- higher risk lowers the score) Tj
T*
(- lambda controls how strongly risk is penalized) Tj
T*
T*
(### `estimateRiskReturn\(...\)`) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
