(This method estimates expected return and expected risk for each asset.) Tj
T*
T*
(It:) Tj
T*
T*
(- fetches price history using `priceService.getHistory\(symbol\)`) Tj
T*
(- extracts close prices) Tj
T*
(- calculates historical return) Tj
T*
(- calculates daily volatility) Tj
T*
(- annualizes volatility) Tj
T*
(- blends historical return with the holding's existing profit percentage) Tj
T*
T*
(If historical data is unavailable, the code falls back to simpler holding-level metrics.) Tj
T*
T*
(### `lambdaForRiskTolerance\(...\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(This maps the user's risk setting into a risk penalty:) Tj
T*
T*
(- low risk -> stronger penalty on risk) Tj
T*
(- medium risk -> balanced penalty) Tj
T*
(- high risk -> lighter penalty on risk) Tj
T*
T*
(This is how the optimizer adapts to different investor preferences.) Tj
T*
T*
(### `adjustReturnForObjective\(...\)` and `adjustRiskForObjective\(...\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(These methods modify return and risk scores depending on the selected investment objective:) Tj
T*
T*
(- growth) Tj
T*
(- balanced) Tj
T*
(- low-risk) Tj
T*
T*
(For example, a growth objective boosts return emphasis, while a low-risk objective penalizes) Tj
T*
( risk more heavily.) Tj
T*
T*
(### `computeTargetWeights\(...\)`) Tj
T*
T*
(This is where the recommended portfolio allocation is produced.) Tj
T*
T*
(The method:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Ranks assets by score.) Tj
T*
(2. Keeps the top N assets based on `maxHoldings`.) Tj
T*
(3. Shifts scores into positive space.) Tj
T*
(4. Normalizes them into target weights that sum to 100%.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
